"payments-worker", "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01R57epbp6zeadtxoMgd7Lf1", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-api", "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled payments-worker back to v3.3.0 and opened the SEV2. The worker has recovered, but payments-api is still failing at 18%.\n\n- **Rollback:** payments-worker went from v3.4.0 back to v3.3.0, its last release that was healthy in production. It's now on v3.3.0 in us-east, us-west and eu-west, marked healthy, and its error rate dropped from 18% to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** I opened **INC-0001** (SEV2, payments-worker) and on-call has been paged. The summary includes the bad release, the rollback and the payments-api errors.\n\nI checked payments-api right after the rollback and its error rate hasn't changed. It may still be catching up (retries, queue backlog), or its own release, v5.1.0, may have a separate problem. That release is marked \"degraded,\" and its last healthy version is v5.0.0.\n\nI haven't touched payments-api, since you said its errors come from the worker. If it hasn't recovered in a few minutes, I can roll it back to v5.0.0. That version was healthy in production, so it doesn't need change-manager approval. I also can't update incidents with these tools, so on-call should add the payments-api status to INC-0001.", "type": "text"}]}]}